:- module(trhe, [foo/3]).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

% The positive twin of typecheck_rigid_head_overload. The same
% polymorphic head, but the guard `integer(X)` is an evidence form:
% the rule body runs only where X is an integer, so the fact pins the
% head occurrence's rigid T := int. Y shares that T, and `X > Y`
% resolves at int (spec §Guard-Derived Type Evidence §What evidence
% does).
:- chr_constraint foo(T, T, any).

foo(X, Y, R) <=> integer(X) | R is X > Y.
